# ======================= STIG rule tables (refresh: spec 03) ==========================
# Data-driven hardening depth from the DISA STIG for IBM AIX 7.x (public domain). The
# rule engine evaluates these rows against live evidence; see eval_fileperms and
# docs/COVERAGE.md (STIG depth section) for the transcribed/deferred accounting.
#
# R_FILEPERM — static file permission/ownership rules.
#   V-ID|path|owner|group|maxmode
#   owner/group are NUMERIC ids (root=0, system group=0, security=7, cron=8, audit=10, bin=2)
#   to avoid name-resolution variance; ls is captured with -n. maxmode is the strictest
#   allowed octal ("or less permissive") — evaluated as a mask (a stricter file PASSES),
#   never equality. A path absent from the box is NA (many are optional subsystems), not FAIL.
#   An EMPTY owner/group/maxmode field means the rule does not address that attribute (each
#   AIX STIG V-ID mandates one attribute; owner root=0, group system=0, security=7).
#   Transcribed verbatim from STIGQter V2R2 Check/Fix text (V-215xxx) and stigviewer
#   authoritative rule titles (V-245xxx, one Tenable-confirmed); see docs/COVERAGE.md
#   for the transcribed/deferred accounting and per-rule provenance.
R_FILEPERM="
V-215269|/etc/inetd.conf|0|0|0644
V-215272|/etc/ntp.conf|0||
V-215273|/etc/ntp.conf||0|
V-215281|/etc/ntp.conf|||0640
V-215274|/etc/group|0||
V-215275|/etc/group||7|
V-215282|/etc/group|||0644
